@startuml fork-add-patch
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #E8F0FE
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #4285F4
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF9C4
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #FBC02D
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF9C4
skinparam NoteBorderColor #FBC02D

title Adding a New Patch (from upstream PR or own feature)

|Phase 1: Develop|

start

:Branch from dev.patch
``git checkout dev.patch``
``git checkout -b feature/xxx``;

:Develop normally
Edit files, commit freely
``npm run dev`` for hot reload;

:Verify build
``npm run build:dev``
``go build ./pkg/...``
``go test ./pkg/...``;

|Phase 2: Convert to .patch|

repeat
  :Generate .patch file
  ``git diff upstream/main...HEAD > .github/patches/NNN-desc.patch``;

  :Test patch applies cleanly
  ``git checkout dev.patch``
  ``git checkout upstream/main -- <modified files>``
  ``git apply --check NNN-desc.patch``;
repeat while (Patch doesn't apply cleanly?\nRebase feature branch onto\nlatest upstream and retry) is (yes)
-> no;

:Apply for real
``git apply NNN-desc.patch``;

:Verify idempotency
``git apply --reverse --check NNN-desc.patch``;

if (Reverse check passes?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Patch is not cleanly
  reversible — fix it;
  stop
endif

|Phase 3: Register|

:Add modified files to PATCHED_FILES
in sync-upstream-and-fix.yml
(new files don't need listing);

:Add entry to ALREADY_INTEGRATED
in generate_upstream_prs.py;

:Update workflow commit message
to list the new patch;

:Commit and push
``git add -A``
``git commit -m "feat: integrate ..."``
``git push origin dev.patch``;

stop

@enduml
